</span> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 12:4\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.12.4\">Ec 12:4</a> <em>the daughters of song</em>, i.e. songs, melodious notes; <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת־בְּלִיַּעַל</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 1:16\" href=\"/I_Samuel.1.16\">1 S 1:16</a> v. <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, בְּלִיַּ֫עַל\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_בְּלִיַּ֫עַל\">בְּלִיַּעַל</a> sub <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, בְּלִיַּ֫עַל\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_בְּלִיַּ֫עַל\">בלה</a>."}], "num": "5."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "<span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת יַעֲנָה</span> = <em>ostrich</em> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 11:16\" href=\"/Leviticus.11.16\">Lv 11:16</a> = <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 14:15\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.14.15\">Dt 14:15</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנוֹת יַעֲנָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 30:29\" href=\"/Job.30.29\">Jb 30:29</a> <a data-ref=\"Micah 1:8\" href=\"/Micah.1.8\">Mi 1:8</a> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 13:21\" href=\"/Isaiah.13.21\">Is 13:21</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 34:13\" href=\"/Isaiah.34.13\">34:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 43:20\" href=\"/Isaiah.43.20\">43:20</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 50:39\" href=\"/Jeremiah.50.39\">Je 50:39</a> (v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, יַעֲנָה\" href=\"/BDB,_יַעֲנָה\", dir=\"rtl\">יַעֲנָה</a>); <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת־עַיִן</span> <em>pupil of the eye</em> <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 2:18\" href=\"/Lamentations.2.18\">La 2:18</a> cf. Ethiopic ብንተ ዐይን v. also <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, אִישׁוֹן\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_אִישׁוֹן\">אִישׁוֹן</a>."}], "all_cited": true, "num": "6."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "fig. <span dir=\"rtl\">לַעֲלוּקָה שְׁתֵּי בָנוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 30:15\" href=\"/Proverbs.30.15\">Pr 30:15</a> <em>two daughters</em> (i.e. Sh<sup>e</sup>ʾôl & the barren womb, cf. Comm.)"}], "all_cited": true, "num": "7."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "of vine = <em>branch</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">בָּנוֹת צָֽעֲדָה עֲלֵי־שׁוּר</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 49:22\" href=\"/Genesis.49.22\">Gn 49:22</a> cf. Di & v. sub <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, בֵּן²\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_בֵּן²\">בֵּן</a>."}], "all_cited": true, "num": "8."}, {"senses": [{"definition": "as n. relat. (all P), of age of woman <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת־תִּשְׁעִים שָׁנָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 17:17\" href=\"/Genesis.17.17\">Gn 17:17</a>; of ewe-lamb <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת־שְׁנָתָהּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 14:10\" href=\"/Leviticus.14.10\">Lv 14:10</a> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 6:14\" href=\"/Numbers.6.14\">Nu 6:14</a>; of she-goat <em>id.</em> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 15:27\" href=\"/Numbers.15.27\">Nu 15:27</a>. Cf. <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, בֵּן²\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_בֵּן²\">בֵּן</a>. <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, בֵּן²\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_בֵּן²\">9</a>—ii. <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת</span> v. <a ,=\"\" data-ref=\"BDB, בתת\" dir=\"rtl\" href=\"/BDB,_בתת\">בתת</a> p. 144."}], "all_cited": true, "num": "9."}]}, "rid": "BDB01311", "strong_numbers": ["1004", "1323", "1324", "1325"], "next_hw": "בַּת־רַבִּים", "prev_hw": "בְּנִ֑ינוּ", "ordinal": "I.", "occurrences": "587", "quotes": [], "GK": ["1426", "1427", "1428"], "TWOT": ["241", "254b", "2644", "298a"], "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "BDB Dictionary", "language": "heb.biblical", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "BDB Dictionary", "attribution": "F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs", "index_title": "BDB", "version_title": "A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete": true}}, {"headword": "בַּת²", "parent_lexicon": "BDB Dictionary", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": "<em>daughter</em> v. sub <a data-ref=\"BDB, בֵּן\" href=\"/BDB,_בֵּן\", dir=\"rtl\">בן</a>."}]}, "rid": "BDB01532", "strong_numbers": ["1004", "1323", "1324", "1325"], "next_hw": "בַּת³", "prev_hw": "בֹּשֶׁת", "ordinal": "I.", "quotes": [], "GK": ["1426", "1427", "1428"], "TWOT": ["241", "254b", "2644", "298a"], "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "BDB Dictionary", "language": "heb.biblical", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "BDB Dictionary", "attribution": "F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs", "index_title": "BDB", "version_title": "A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete": true}}, {"headword": "בַּת³", "parent_lexicon": "BDB Dictionary", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": "<em>bath</em> (a measure), <span dir=\"rtl\">בָּתָה</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּתָּה</span> v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, בתת\" href=\"/BDB,_בתת\", dir=\"rtl\">בתת</a>."}]}, "rid": "BDB01533", "strong_numbers": ["1004", "1323", "1324", "1325"], "next_hw": "בְּתוּאֵל", "prev_hw": "בַּת²", "ordinal": "II.", "quotes": [], "GK": ["1426", "1427", "1428"], "TWOT": ["241", "254b", "2644", "298a"], "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "BDB Dictionary", "language": "heb.biblical", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "BDB Dictionary", "attribution": "F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs", "index_title": "BDB", "version_title": "A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete": true}}, {"headword": "בַּת⁴", "parent_lexicon": "BDB Dictionary", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": "<strong>n.m.</strong> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 45:14\" href=\"/Ezekiel.45.14\">Ez 45:14</a> (f. <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 5:10\" href=\"/Isaiah.5.10\">Is 5:10</a>) <strong>bath (</strong>Thes al. from above √ in sense of <em>define, measure;</em> cf. τέμνω; Lag<sup>Or</sup>. <sup>ii. 10 f.</sup> makes = <span dir=\"rtl\">בדת</span>, = <span dir=\"rtl\">בד</span> + fem. ת; cf. Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܒܕ</span>, instrument for pressing olives; cf. Epiphan. βάδος = ἐλαιοτριβεῖον; & βάδος also Hesych. Jos<sup>Ant.</sup> viii, 2, 9 but ed. Niese βάτους, βάτος<strong>)</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">בּ׳</span> abs. <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 5:10\" href=\"/Isaiah.5.10\">Is 5:10</a> + 6 times; (<span dir=\"rtl\">בָּ֑ת</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 45:11\" href=\"/Ezekiel.45.11\">Ez 45:11</a>) cstr. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 45:10\" href=\"/Ezekiel.45.10\">Ez 45:10</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּתִּים</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 2:9\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.2.9\">2 Ch 2:9</a><sup>(×2)</sup> + 3 times;—a liquid measure = <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵיפָה</span> of dry measure, each being 1/10 <span dir=\"rtl\">חֹמֶר</span> (q.v.) <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 45:11\" href=\"/Ezekiel.45.11\">Ez 45:11</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 45:14\" href=\"/Ezekiel.45.14\">14</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; also <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 5:10\" href=\"/Isaiah.5.10\">Is 5:10</a> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 7:26\" href=\"/I_Kings.7.26\">1 K 7:26</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 7:38\" href=\"/I_Kings.7.38\">38</a> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 2:9\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.2.9\">2 Ch 2:9</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 4:5\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.4.5\">4:5</a> + <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 45:14\" href=\"/Ezekiel.45.14\">Ez 45:14</a><sup>(×2)</sup> (4 times in this v., Co del. <em>a</em> & <em>d</em>). <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 45:10\" href=\"/Ezekiel.45.10\">Ez 45:10</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת־צֶדֶק</span> <em>a righteous</em> (right, accurate, full) <em>bath</em> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">אֵיפַת־צֶדֶק</span>). The actual size of bath (= ephah) is appar. c. 40 litres (= Attic <em>metretes</em> cf. Jos<sup>Ant.</sup> viii, 2, 9; = 39.39 lit. cf. Boeckh<sup> Metrol. Untersuch. 259 f.</sup>; v. also J. Brandis<sup> Münz- Mass- u. Gewichtswesen 29 f.</sup> Smith<sup> Dict. Bible, art. Weights & Measures</sup> Ri<sup>HWB 934 f.</sup>).—i. <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת</span> v. sub <a data-ref=\"BDB, בֵּן²\" href=\"/BDB,_בֵּן²\", dir=\"rtl\">בֵּן</a>."}]}, "rid": "BDB01547", "strong_numbers": ["1004", "1323", "1324", "1325"], "next_hw": "בַּתָּה", "prev_hw": "בתת", "all_cited": true, "ordinal": "II.", "quotes": [], "GK": ["1426", "1427", "1428"], "TWOT": ["241", "254b", "2644", "298a"], "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "BDB Dictionary", "language": "heb.biblical", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "BDB Dictionary", "attribution": "F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs", "index_title": "BDB", "version_title": "A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete": true}}, {"headword": "צִיּוֹן", "parent_lexicon": "BDB Dictionary", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": "<strong>n.pr.loc.</strong> Σ(ε)ιων; Ṣîyyôn, Zion <strong>(</strong>Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܨܶܗܝܘܿܢ</span>, older form, according to Lag<sup>BN 84, cf. 198</sup><strong>)</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">צ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 5:7\" href=\"/II_Samuel.5.7\">2 S 5:7</a> +; <span dir=\"rtl\">צִיּו֫נָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 4:6\" href=\"/Jeremiah.4.6\">Je 4:6</a>;—stronghold (of Jebusites), <span dir=\"rtl\">מְצֻדַת צ׳</span> captured by David, and made his residence <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 5:7\" href=\"/II_Samuel.5.7\">2 S 5:7</a> = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 11:5\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.11.5\">1 Ch 11:5</a> (both + <span dir=\"rtl\">הִיא עִיר דָּוִד</span>), on S. part of E. hill of Jerusalem, distinct from site of temple <a data-ref=\"I Kings 8:1\" href=\"/I_Kings.8.1\">1 K 8:1</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 5:2\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.5.2\">2 Ch 5:2</a> (both <span dir=\"rtl\">מֵעִיר ד׳ הִיא צ׳</span>), not elsewhere in narrative, but often in poets and proph.: as name of Jerus., from political point of view (sometimes = inhabitants), <a data-ref=\"Amos 6:7\" href=\"/Amos.6.7\">Am 6:7</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר־שֹׁמְרוֹן</span>), ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרוּשָׁלַםִ</span> <a data-ref=\"Micah 3:10\" href=\"/Micah.3.10\">Mi 3:10</a>, <a data-ref=\"Micah 3:12\" href=\"/Micah.3.12\">12</a> = <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 26:18\" href=\"/Jeremiah.26.18\">Je 26:18</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 4:3\" href=\"/Isaiah.4.3\">Is 4:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 30:19\" href=\"/Isaiah.30.19\">30:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 40:9\" href=\"/Isaiah.40.9\">40:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 41:27\" href=\"/Isaiah.41.27\">41:27</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 52:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.52.1\">52:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 62:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.62.1\">62:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 64:9\" href=\"/Isaiah.64.9\">64:9</a> <a data-ref=\"Zephaniah 3:16\" href=\"/Zephaniah.3.16\">Zp 3:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 1:14\" href=\"/Zechariah.1.14\">Zc 1:14</a>, <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 1:17\" href=\"/Zechariah.1.17\">17</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 51:20\" href=\"/Psalms.51.20\">ψ 51:20</a> and <span dir=\"rtl\">(בַּת־צ׳)</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 52:2\" href=\"/Isaiah.52.2\">Is 52:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Micah 4:8\" href=\"/Micah.4.8\">Mi 4:8</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת־יְרוּשׁ׳</span>), <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 2:13\" href=\"/Lamentations.2.13\">La 2:13</a> (‖ id.), also <span dir=\"rtl\">(יוֹשֶׁבֶת צ׳)</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 51:35\" href=\"/Jeremiah.51.35\">Je 51:35</a>; = Jerus. also <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 14:32\" href=\"/Isaiah.14.32\">Is 14:32</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 33:5\" href=\"/Isaiah.33.5\">33:5</a> +, so especially in phr. <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנוֹת צ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 3:16\" href=\"/Isaiah.3.16\">Is 3:16</a>, <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 3:17\" href=\"/Isaiah.3.17\">17</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 4:4\" href=\"/Isaiah.4.4\">4:4</a>; <a data-ref=\"Song of Songs 3:11\" href=\"/Song_of_Songs.3.11\">Ct 3:11</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנֵי צ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 4:2\" href=\"/Lamentations.4.2\">La 4:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joel 2:23\" href=\"/Joel.2.23\">Jo 2:23</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 149:2\" href=\"/Psalms.149.2\">ψ 149:2</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">יִשְׂרָאֵל</span>), cf. <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 9:13\" href=\"/Zechariah.9.13\">Zc 9:13</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">יָֽלְדָה צ׳ אֶת־בָּנֶיהָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 66:8\" href=\"/Isaiah.66.8\">Is 66:8</a>, and even <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר־צ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"II Kings 19:31\" href=\"/II_Kings.19.31\">2 K 19:31</a> = <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 37:32\" href=\"/Isaiah.37.32\">Is 37:32</a> (both ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרוּשׁ׳</span>), <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 29:8\" href=\"/Isaiah.29.8\">Is 29:8</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">אֲרִיאֵל</span> v <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 29:7\" href=\"/Isaiah.29.7\">7</a>), <a data-ref=\"Obadiah 1:17\" href=\"/Obadiah.1.17\">Ob 17</a>, <a data-ref=\"Obadiah 1:21\" href=\"/Obadiah.1.21\">21</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 48:12\" href=\"/Psalms.48.12\">ψ 48:12</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">בְּנוֹת יֶהוֹדָה</span>), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 125:1\" href=\"/Psalms.125.1\">125:1</a>; so also <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר־בַּת צ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 16:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.16.1\">Is 16:1</a> and <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 10:32\" href=\"/Isaiah.10.32\">10:32</a> Qr (Kt <span dir=\"rtl\">בית</span>: ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">גִּבְעַת־יְרוּשׁ׳</span>); cf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְרוֹם־צ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 31:12\" href=\"/Jeremiah.31.12\">Je 31:12</a>; in foll. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר־צ׳</span> might refer to temple-hill <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 10:12\" href=\"/Isaiah.10.12\">Is 10:12</a> (+ <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרוּשׁ׳</span>), <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 31:4\" href=\"/Isaiah.31.4\">31:4</a> (+ <span dir=\"rtl\">גִּבְעָתָהּ</span> = <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרוּשׁ׳</span> v <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 31:5\" href=\"/Isaiah.31.5\">5</a>), <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 5:18\" href=\"/Lamentations.5.18\">La 5:18</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joel 3:5\" href=\"/Joel.3.5\">Jo 3:5</a> (+ <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרוּשׁ׳</span>); specif. of Jerus. as abode of <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> and place of his worship <a data-ref=\"Amos 1:2\" href=\"/Amos.1.2\">Am 1:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 31:9\" href=\"/Isaiah.31.9\">Is 31:9</a>; <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 8:3\" href=\"/Zechariah.8.3\">Zc 8:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Micah 4:2\" href=\"/Micah.4.2\">Mi 4:2</a> = <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 2:3\" href=\"/Isaiah.2.3\">Is 2:3</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joel 4:16\" href=\"/Joel.4.16\">Jo 4:16</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 102:22\" href=\"/Psalms.102.22\">ψ 102:22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 135:21\" href=\"/Psalms.135.21\">135:21</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 147:12\" href=\"/Psalms.147.12\">147:12</a> (all ‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרוּשׁ׳</span>), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 76:3\" href=\"/Psalms.76.3\">76:3</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">שָׁלֵם</span>); partic. of sanctuary <a data-ref=\"Psalms 20:3\" href=\"/Psalms.20.3\">20:3</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">קֹדֶשׁ</span>), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 14:7\" href=\"/Psalms.14.7\">14:7</a> = <a data-ref=\"Psalms 53:7\" href=\"/Psalms.53.7\">53:7</a> +; of Jerus. <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר־צ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 48:3\" href=\"/Psalms.48.3\">ψ 48:3</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">קִרְיַת מֶלֶךְ רָ֑ב</span>), <a data-ref=\"Psalms 78:68\" href=\"/Psalms.78.68\">78:68</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">שֵׁבֶט יְהוּדָה</span>), <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 24:23\" href=\"/Isaiah.24.23\">Is 24:23</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">יְרוּשׁ׳</span>), etc.; <span dir=\"rtl\">הַרֲרֵי צ׳</span> in same sense †<a data-ref=\"Psalms 133:3\" href=\"/Psalms.133.3\">ψ 133:3</a>; particularly of sanctuary <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 4:5\" href=\"/Isaiah.4.5\">Is 4:5</a> and (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר־קָדְשִׁי</span>) <a data-ref=\"Joel 2:1\" href=\"/Joel.2.1\">Jo 2:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Joel 4:17\" href=\"/Joel.4.17\">4:17</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">צ׳ הַר־קָדְשִׁי</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 2:6\" href=\"/Psalms.2.6\">ψ 2:6</a> is seat of king.—Vid. also <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת־צ׳</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר־צ׳</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ישֶׁבֶת צ׳</span>, sub <a data-ref=\"BDB, בַּת\" href=\"/BDB,_בַּת\", dir=\"rtl\">בַּת</a>, <a data-ref=\"BDB, הַר²\" href=\"/BDB,_הַר²\", dir=\"rtl\">הַר</a>, <a data-ref=\"BDB, יָשַׁב\" href=\"/BDB,_יָשַׁב\", dir=\"rtl\">יָשַׁב</a>."}]}, "rid": "BDB08367", "strong_numbers": ["6726"], "next_hw": "צָיוֹן²", "prev_hw": "צָיוֹן", "occurrences": "154", "quotes": [], "GK": ["7482"], "TWOT": ["1910"], "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "BDB Dictionary", "language": "heb.biblical", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "BDB Dictionary", "attribution": "F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs", "index_title": "BDB", "version_title": "A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete": true}}, {"headword": "בַּת", "parent_lexicon": "BDB Aramaic Dictionary", "content": {"senses": [{"definition": "<strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>bath</strong>, liquid measure <strong>(</strong>𝔗; perhaps loan-word from BH ii. <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּת</span>, √ <span dir=\"rtl\">בתת</span><strong>)</strong>;—pl. abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּתִּין</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 7:22\" href=\"/Ezra.7.22\">Ezr 7:22</a><sup>(×2)</sup>."}]}, "rid": "BDBA0153", "strong_numbers": ["1004", "1323", "1324", "1325"], "next_hw": "בָּת", "prev_hw": "בְּשַׂר", "all_cited": true, "brackets": "first_word", "quotes": [], "GK": ["1426", "1427", "1428"], "TWOT": ["241", "254b", "2644", "298a"], "parent_lexicon_details": {"name": "BDB Aramaic Dictionary", "language": "ara.biblical", "to_language": "eng", "text_categories": [], "source": "BDB Dictionary", "attribution": "F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs", "index_title": "BDB Aramaic", "version_title": "A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906", "version_lang": "en", "should_autocomplete": true}}]